<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Solidarnosk	unloading   corn screening  6,577     U.S.</p>
<p>Southern Venture unloading   wheat	    35,643     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   7,355</p>
<p>Peleduy	    arrived     sunflower	 1,860     Europe</p>
<p>Stella Tingas    arrived     barley	   20,984     U.S.</p>
<p>Semion Rundov    arrived     sunflower meal  1,874     Europe</p>
<p>Vasily Bojenko   arrived     maize grits     2,400     Europe</p>
<p>Almira	     03/02	 sunflower	 1,965     Europe</p>
<p>Spiridon	   04/02	 sorghum	  13,985     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	     7,926</p>
<p>				     soya		4,114</p>
<p>Vera		 05/02	 wheat	    21,950     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  11,541</p>
<p>N. Krivorutsko   07/02	 maize grits     2,200     Europe</p>
